iberately broken; migration 0006 applied and its claim, finalize, fail, stale re-claim and grant behaviour was exercised on a scratch Postgres 16 without pgvector (the vector column replaced by `real[]`, `match_chunks` skipped). Not verified: a real HTTP 429 or 5xx from Gemini (the retry path is covered only by simulated errors); the `supabase-js` call shapes under the real type definitions in Claude's sandbox (the owner's typecheck covers them); a GitHub Actions run on this change; and the effect of seeding on `supabase/tests/security.sql` T00, which asserts exactly 2 public documents and 14 chunks. Known limits and follow-ups: the placeholder Northwind and Fabrikam rows in `supabase/seed.sql` were not replaced (the 2026-11-01 Task 0.9 entry expected Task 1.6 to do that), so a seeded local database has four public documents and the two real ones are the only ones with real embeddings; a run that outlives the 10-minute stale window can overlap a second run (the late run gets `claim_lost` at finalize, but may still have written chunks that the new claim's wipe does not cover); a chunk that begins with the literal embedding prefix is rejected by the adapter and fails as `internal_error` (very unlikely); the 15 s and 30 s waits, the 10-chunk batches and the 10 s pause are not tuned against a real quota; the 1200 and 150 chunking defaults are still provisional until the Slice 2 eval. Not built: the `/api/ingest` route, upload UI and `maxDuration` choice (Slice 4), the shared admin client (Task 1.7), and `security.sql` tests for the ingestion functions (Task 4.2).
